opengl32: queue simple immediate-mode calls of 32-bit programs and send them in one unix call.

Soju patch (LGPL-2.1-or-later, like Wine). A 32-bit process switches to 64-bit code and back for every
unix call, which is slow under Rosetta 2. GoldSrc games (Counter-Strike 1.6, Half-Life, Sven Co-op) make
about 45,000 OpenGL calls per frame, nearly all glVertex/glTexCoord/glColor/glBegin/glEnd. Calls without
results or pointers are queued per thread and replayed in order by one unix call before any other
GL/WGL call. SOJU_GL_BATCH=0 turns it off (#153).

